## 1 · Principles (each one forced by a finding)

| # | Principle | Finding that forces it |
|---|---|---|
| P1 | **Clusters are crates.** The compiler enforces the dependency law. There is no convention and no comment-link. | CM: 1 crate, 17 flat mods, 0 cluster checks in gate, **7 undeclared edges incl. worker→actions (K2→K6 inversion)** (CM's text says 6; its own table lists 7, service→worker omitted from Stage 2; ERRATA) *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-18)*; DR:1887 deferred the split to post-tag, so v4 is where it lands |
| P2 | **State machines are types.** Every durable state is a contracts enum, and one pure `transition(State, Event) -> Result<State, Illegal>` exists per machine. The store writes only what `transition` returns. | AR:1 task state is a `String` written at ≥9 sites with no transition fn; §5c lists the v3 write sites |
| P3 | **One cancellation source.** | AR:1 cancellation held twice (`tasks.cancellation` flag + state `cancellation_requested`, `store.rs:2239-2245`) |
| P4 | **One verdict authority.** The ledger verdict is `verdict_of(check::decide)`. Nothing else produces a verdict. | AR:3 / MA:11 ledger takes live_verifier's verdict; `decide` cannot PASS (3 identities — Collector, Locks, Standards — hard-wired `None`/Unavailable in `app/u64_receipt.rs:136-145` `identities()`; the earlier cite `check/decision.rs:46,97,120` names the `Unavailable` variants, not the wiring *(rev 2026-10-01, V2 fix 10)*). Lands in **phase P3**, before phase P4's first host record *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-13)* |
| P5 | **One door per rule.** Every bound, limit and vocabulary has exactly one definition site, and every other site reads it. | AR:5 run limit spelled 4× (`mod.rs:713/737`, `native.rs:394`, `process.rs:541`) *(cited)*; frame limit literal at `store.rs:1236` + `coordinator.rs:53`; AR:21 bash clamps what the engine refuses; AR:8/9/16/17 duplicate outboxes, join engines, omission vocabularies and shape checks. Measured by the one-door census, which prints `duplicate_sites=N`; the gate is its reader *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-17)* |
| P6 | **Ports live in contracts.** A cluster exposes a trait in `hee4-contracts`, and app wires the implementation. No cluster reaches into another's state. | CM: service→store (writes directly), worker→actions; AR:6 "return a validated observation for app to commit" |
| P7 | **Policy/IO split (F95).** Every decision is a pure fn over values, and the I/O shell is thin. | Already proven in v3: `dispatcher.rs:245,289,299,316` (`backup_due`, `headroom`, `budget_decision`, `headroom_decision`); RR build-01 (move rule (a)/(b) policy out of `observe()`); AR:6 LocalProbe Option-soup |
| P8 | **Acquisition is bounded, and the derived set is bounded too.** | RR security-2 (`native.rs:1074` fd readlink bytes unbounded); DR:1892 roster observations capped at 4096 **globally, never pruned** (`store/roster.rs:615`, `contracts/roster.rs:9`) *(cited)*; AR:16 unbounded Permit; MA:2 EventCursorV1 unbounded |
| P9 | **One idempotent-operation primitive.** Replay is derived from `Effect::mutates()` (`actions.rs:485`). | AR SYS rec 2; `INSERT INTO operations` at 4 sites (`store.rs:1254,1651,1802`, `store/roster.rs:271`) + 3 `replayed_*` fns (`store.rs:1268,1281,1294`) |
| P10 | **Dispatch by owner registry.** Dispatch never goes through a string match. | AR:20 + SYS rec 1: `actions/control.rs:479` `match action.id`, `UNSERVED` list `:418`, 3 lists must agree; `Owner` already exists on every `Action` (`actions.rs:504`) |
| P11 | **Every written row has a reader in production, or it is not written.** | AR SYS HIGH: outbox inserted (C2: 2 sites) and never delivered (`pending_delivery`/`acknowledge_delivery` `store.rs:2032,2054`: 0 production callers); budget Ledger 0 callers (AR:4) |
| P12 | **Advisory typed judgment (Jev) is a port behind a `DataClass` boundary.** Advice is never authority. | JM §4: 14 JUDGMENT vs 145 EXACT + 42 THRESHOLD sites; `Advised<T>{decision, advice, agreed}`; engine data held for Luke's grant (JM §5) |
| P13 | **One spawn door and one egress door**, each in its own crate: spawn in `hee4-host` (K0h), egress in `hee4-egress` (K0e), which only `hee4-app` (K6) may depend on *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-12)*. | IM §6: `process.rs:547` is the one spawn door, but numerical→worker and service→worker edges (CM) exist only to reach it |
| P14 | **Every gate input comes from the world it certifies** (host records are declared gate inputs). | RR build-01/tests-8 (the gate pinned `host=0` on a copy without `evidence/host/`) |
| P15 | **Catalogues are pinned by content, not count.** | AR SYS MED (JSON schema vs CATALOGUE pinned by count only); AR:11 two tool-projection authorities |

