## 3 · Flow map

### 3a · Inbound command path (v3 baseline, 21 hops, re-derived at b5367bc; see C3)

| # | v3 hop | v3 `file:line` | v4 change |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `habitat-engine <action>` CLI client connects | `main.rs:1147,1175` *(IM)* | K6; binary `hee4` *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-11)* |
| 2 | serve: custody flock, bind 0700/0600 | `control_socket.rs:246,299` | **REUSE verbatim** |
| 3 | accept loop | `control_socket.rs:626,640` | unchanged |
| 4 | peer uid (SO_PEERCRED) | `control_socket.rs:314` | unchanged |
| 5 | admit peer → Principal | `control_socket.rs:326,708` | unchanged |
| 6 | per-principal rate bucket | `control_socket.rs:355,375` | limit constant read from K0 (P5) |
| 7 | connection cap | `control_socket.rs:537,751` | unchanged |
| 8 | `serve_connection` reads one frame | `control_socket.rs:454` | **Reply::Stream arm** added (loop writes N frames until close/cursor end) |
| 9 | `actions::control::serve_composed` | `actions/control.rs:265` | K6 |
| 10 | `wire::receive` (≤1 MiB, version 1) | `contracts/control.rs:1166` | K0; RT S4 fuzz test (Scanner-accept ⇒ serde-accept) kept |
| 11 | replay-expired check | `actions/control.rs:282,313` | **→ K1 idempotent-op primitive** (P9) |
| 12 | admit: catalogue lookup + precondition | `actions/control.rs:343,364` | lookup by content-pinned catalogue (P15) |
| 13 | `dispatch` string match | `actions/control.rs:469,479` | **→ owner registry** `Registry::get(action.owner)` → `&dyn OwnerPort`; UNSERVED list deleted (unserved = no registry entry = refusal by name) |
| 14 | `task::control::submission` parse | `task/control.rs:100` | K1, parse derived from the one field list (AR:14) |
| 15 | `StoreTasks::submit` | `app/tasks.rs:571` | K6 port impl, thin |
| 16 | `Store::submit` bound + insert tasks row + operations row | `store.rs:1234,1249,1254` | bound read from K0 (the `1_048_576` literal at :1236 dies); **operations via the primitive**; state from `transition(∅, Admit)` |
| 17 | dispatcher waits | `dispatcher.rs:896`, `tasks.rs:114` | unchanged |
| 18 | `next_dispatchable` | `store.rs:1439` | Dispatchable carries a typed `TaskState`, not `state == "cancellation_requested"` (`store.rs:1458`; was cited :1457 *(rev 2026-10-01, V2 fix 10)*) |
| 19 | `runtime::drive` → `task::driver::run` | `runtime.rs:937`, `driver.rs:114` | `runtime::lifecycle`; driver uses the guard (AR:15) |
| 20 | begin attempt (`admitted\|repair_pending → running`) | `runtime.rs:2024`, `store.rs:2612,2637,2642` | `transition(Begin)`; roster observation → **retained, per-principal** (DR:1892) |
| 21 | execute → verify → accept (`native::execute`, check, `store.accept`, outbox insert) | `runtime.rs:2134,2226,2336`, `native.rs:1523`, `store.rs:1961,2024` | execute via K2 + K0h; **verify via K4 `decide` only (P4)**: the K6 live-verifier adapter runs the stages and hands observations to `decide`, landed in phase P3 *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-13)*; accept via `transition(Accept)`; outbox insert kept **and now read** (3b.6) |

### 3b · Outbound observation path (v3 baseline, 8 hops)

| # | v3 hop | v3 `file:line` | v4 change |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `task.get` / `task.list` parse | `task/control.rs:525,384` | K1, unchanged |
| 2 | `StoreTasks::get` / `list` | `app/tasks.rs:642,730` | K6 port impl |
| 3 | `Store::get` / `get_by_key` | `store.rs:1345,1327` | state read as `TaskState` enum, not String |
| 4 | evidence view | `app/tasks.rs:415,555` | unchanged |
| 5 | `delivery_of(state, pending, given_up)` | `app/tasks.rs:701,971` | reads a **real** delivered count, so "pending forever" ends |
| 6 | outbox / `events_after` (unserved) | `store.rs:1363,2032,2054` | **served** by `events.subscribe` → K3 delivery policy over K1 rows → `acknowledge_delivery` has a caller; lands in **phase P5** with the outbox reader *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-14)* |
| 7 | reply frame | `actions/control.rs:300` | `Reply::Frame` or `Reply::Stream` |
| 8 | client prints; bash/Pi consume | `main.rs:1175`, `hee3:155` *(IM)* | bash refuses over-limit deadlines instead of clamping (AR:21) |

### 3c · New v4 flows (no v3 hop exists)

| Flow | Path |
|---|---|
| Judgment (held for grant) | ~~K3/K2 consumer~~ the K6 module that owns the decision (candidates, workload, repair; *rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-66, DC-45*) → `Advised<T>` port (K0) → K6 checks `DataClass` against the grant record → K0e egress *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-12)* → K1 `judgments` row (question-set digest, state digest, model, p, tokens) → budget charge through the one charge door. Outage → `UNMEASURED`, and the code decision stands (JM §4.3-4.6) |
| Service observation | K5 probe (pure policy over K0h I/O) → validated `Observation` → K6 commits via K1 (replaces the direct service→store write, AR:6) |
| Roster install | deploy/installer → a K1 internal operation kind (`Owner::Deploy`) (*rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-62, DC-40: at phase P3 only the native-provider's own record is composed through this kind; the general installer is v4.1*), **not** under the wire id `roster.update` (AR SYS HIGH: `native_provider.rs:273` pre-populates that action's idempotency space) |

*(rev 2026-10-01 jev-fit)* NF-JUDGE placement: the Jev fit per decision lives in vault `50 Jev/Jev Fit Map` §3 (the single home of the 51 intersections; query `hee4db highway --jev`).

