## 5 · State map

### 5a · Durable tables (all owned by K1 `hee4-core::store`; v3 `migrations/001-008.sql`)
| Table | v3 origin | Single writer (v4) | Reader(s) | v4 change |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| migration_history, ledger_meta (`mode`) | 001 | store::schema | recovery | v4 starts a fresh migration series at 001 |
| tasks (`state`, `cancellation`, budget cols) | 001, 004 | store via `transition` | task.get/list, dispatcher, herdr, ATLAS D9 | `state` from `TaskState`; **`cancellation` column removed**, cancellation lives in the state (P3); `queued` removed from CHECK (C1); **new `serve_cgroup` column** written at admission from `/proc/self/cgroup` of the admitting `serve`, read by the D9 "used" read-back *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-15)* |
| attempts (`state`, `effect`, `cleanup`) | 001, 006 | store via `attempt::transition` | recovery, runtime | `queued` removed (C1) |
| attempt_bindings, attempt_records, attempt_paths | 005-008 | store | receipt, recovery | keep |
| operations | 001→003 | **the idempotent-op primitive only** | replay | one insert site (P9); installer rows under `Owner::Deploy` (§3c) |
| events | 001 | store | outbox, recovery | keep |
| artifacts, acceptances, acceptance_objects | 001, 006 | store | task.get | keep |
| outbox (`delivered`) | 001 | store (2 insert sites → 1 fn) | **events.subscribe** (new) | delivered/ack now reached (P11) |
| verifications | 001, 006 | store, value = `verdict_of(decide)` | recovery, task.get | P4 |
| task_stops, task_dispositions | 001, 003 | store::terminal / resolve | task.get | keep |
| roster_records, _revisions, _observations, _instances, _instance_history, _pins, _cancel_causes | 001 | store::roster (via app from K2) | K2 eligibility | **retention + per-principal cap** (DR:1892); one TTL policy |
| *(new)* cohort_threads, cohort_reports, dissent_log | — | store (via app from K3) | thread.get/list | v4.2; AR:7 durable owner, append-only dissent |
| *(new)* workflow_steps | — | store | workflows | v4.2; AR:9 step-record table |
| *(new)* service_facts | — | store (via app from K5) | health, service.* | v4.2; AR:6 health rebuildable after restart |
| *(new)* judgments | — | store | calibration (K4), judge.inspect | held; JM §4.4 append-only, digests not state |

### 5b · Enums (all defined in K0 `hee4-contracts`; one definition each)
| Enum | v3 definition(s) | v4 |
|---|---|---|
| TaskState (12 → 11) | `recovery.rs:338` + string CHECK (001:912) + `herdr.rs:617` match | one enum; `queued` dropped |
| AttemptState / Effect / Cleanup | `recovery.rs:308-335` + CHECK (001:951) | one enum each |
| Verdict | `recovery.rs` `Verdict` + `VerificationVerdict` + `VerdictV1State` (`receipt/records.rs:101`) | one enum; AR:1 "verdict names spelled twice" |
| Mode | `recovery.rs` | keep |
| ProviderState, InstanceState | `native.rs:508`, `contracts/roster.rs:388` | move native's to K0 |
| Disposition, ObligationKind | 003 CHECK | enum |
| Join/Blocked, Omission, Report | cohort + workflows (2 vocab), context + skills (2 vocab) | one each (AR:7,9,16); a wire-visible enum is defined in K0, a K3-internal one in K3 (*rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-56, DC-14*) |
| DataClass {public, synthetic, projection, local_private} | — | new (JM §4.3) |

### 5c · TaskState transitions (v3 write sites → v4 `transition(State, Event)`)
| From | Event | To | v3 write site |
|---|---|---|---|
| ∅ | Admit | admitted | `store.rs:1249-1252` |
| admitted, repair_pending | Begin | running | `store.rs:2612,2642` |
| running | Settle{settled, ready} | verifying \| repair_pending | `store.rs:1536` |
| running | Settle{unsettled} | effect_unknown (blocked stays blocked) | `store.rs:1536` |
| ~~running (cancel requested)~~ cancellation_requested (*rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-57, DC-07(b): Cancel on `running` already moved the task here; the attempt keeps running under the attempt machine*) | Settle{settled} | cancellation_requested (self-edge) | `store.rs:1536` |
| verifying | Verdict{Passed} | verifying (awaits accept) | `store/verification.rs:247` |
| verifying | Verdict{Failed} | repair_pending | `store/verification.rs:248` |
| verifying | Verdict{Invalid\|Error\|Timeout} | failed | `store/verification.rs:249-250` |
| verifying | Verdict{unreconciled} | effect_unknown | `store/verification.rs:241-242` |
| verifying | Accept | accepted | `store.rs:2019` |
| any non-waiting | Cancel | cancellation_requested | `store.rs:2244` |
| effect_unknown, blocked | Cancel | *same* (flag only today, `store.rs:2239`) | v4: `CancelRequested` becomes a **field of the waiting variant** (`EffectUnknown{cancel: bool}`), so there is one source (P3) |
| ~~any~~ any non-terminal (*rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-57, DC-07(a)*) | Resolve{quarantine} | blocked | `store.rs:1755,1765` |
| ~~any~~ any non-terminal (*rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-57, DC-07(a)*) | Resolve{abandon} | abandoned \| cancelled | `store.rs:1788` → `terminal::close` |
| admitted, ~~queued~~, repair_pending, ~~failed~~, verifying, cancellation_requested (*rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-57, DC-06, DC-34: `queued` no longer exists; Stop on terminal `failed` is `Illegal`; admitted, repair_pending and verifying → failed; cancellation_requested → cancelled*) | Stop | failed \| cancelled | `store/terminal.rs:133-136,210-214` |
| — | startup reconcile | per recovery policy | `store/recovery.rs` (REUSE) |

Terminal: accepted, failed, cancelled, abandoned. Every other pair is `Illegal`, and a property test enumerates all 11×|Event| pairs against this table. The table's source is this list of v3 write sites, which is **not independent of the code** (CLAUDE.md F113). The independent check is the v3 ledger's own CHECK constraints plus recorded v3 event logs. *(rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-57, DC-37)* The one legality home is K1 `task::machine::transition` / `attempt_transition` (no K0 transition table). The constraints are copied read-only to `~/hee4-evidence/reference/v3-records/v3-migration-00{1,2,3}.sql`. The pairs derived from them are in vault `16 System Maps/State and Transition Map` §2c. They decide what the schema can decide: the target sets, one closing record per task, one verdict per attempt and one unsettled attempt per task. A CHECK cannot relate two rows, so the remaining pairs rest on this table and the terminal line. No recorded v3 event log exists in v4, so that half is UNMEASURED.

