## 7 · Design detail: elaboration, not authority *(rev 2026-10-01, the design set)*
Per-module logic and flows, schematics, and the API, socket, command, loop and flow maps live in the v4 vault design set. **This ULTRAMAP stays the authority.** Where a design note and this file disagree, this file wins, and the disagreement goes to the design conflict register.
- **Entry:** [Module Design Index](obsidian://open?vault=herdr-engineering-engine-v4.vault&file=15%20Module%20Design%2F00%20-%20Module%20Design%20Index): 53 modules mapped to their design sections and cards, and the design conflict register ~~of 22 distinct conflicts DC-01…DC-22~~ (DC-01…DC-44, 44 rows on 2026-10-01; `hee4db q 'SELECT status_class, count(*) FROM design_conflicts GROUP BY 1'`) *(rev 2026-10-01 alignment)*; later DC-01…DC-46, all RESOLVED by V4-55…V4-66 *(rev 2026-10-01 funnel audit)*.
- **Elaborations by section:**
  - §2 crate map → `16 System Maps/System Schematic`
  - §3 flows → `End-to-End Flow Traces` (E2E-01…12)
  - §4a/§4c → `Socket and IPC Map` (S-1…S-11) and `Command Map`
  - §4b → `API Map` (22 actions)
  - §5 → `State and Transition Map`
  - §6 → `Anti-Bloat Budget`
  - runtime loops → `Workflow and Loop Map` (RL-1…11, DW-1…7)
- **Per-module working procedure and lessons** *(rev 2026-10-01)*: repo `.claude/skills/hee4-module-slice` (DW-1, after "start coding") and `.claude/skills/hee4-lessons` (AP/EX/D/L/spells by trigger); index `.claude/README.md`; restart `~/handoffs/HEE4_RESTART.md`.
- **Shared vocabulary:** [MODULE-DESIGN-BRIEF.md](file:///var/home/Louranicas/hee4-evidence/design/MODULE-DESIGN-BRIEF.md).
- **Amendments the design set proposes to this file, awaiting ratification (H-27):** *(rev 2026-10-01 alignment: generated; replaces the hand-written list, which named DC-06…DC-09 and a struck DC-01)*
  Generated by `hee4db highway --um-amendments --md`: every open row of the design conflict register (vault `15 Module Design/00 - Module Design Index`) whose Conflict or Status text cites "UM §" or "UM-P". That one rule is shared by the generator and `hee4db check` (`check=alignment_um`). Do not edit between the markers; change the register, run `hee4db ingest`, regenerate. Closed rows (e.g. DC-01, applied under V4-13) drop out.

